# A savestate loaded mid-hazard-death must restore the clean hero, not the death's transient state. A lava death
# disables the hero's renderer, moves it to a non-colliding layer (2) and flips the body Kinematic; the respawn
# coroutine normally undoes that. Load the Tut_01 boundary 40 frames into the death — before the respawn, and late
# enough that its coroutine's owner (the hazard object) is destroyed by the load's scene reload, so nothing cleans up
# afterwards. Without the fix the transient sticks: the hero stays invisible on a non-colliding layer and falls
# through the floor. One assert bundles the restored gameplay state (visible, on the player layer, dynamic body) so a
# failure shows every field at once.
load Tut_01 47.73 4.57
   1
SaveSavestate, {scratch}.boundary.json
load Bone_East_08 97.29 7.06
Set, HeroController.playerData.health, 5
   1,L,J
  25,L
  40
LoadSavestate, {scratch}.boundary.json
   1
   8
Assert, Equal, "renderer=True layer=9 body=Dynamic", "renderer={HeroController.renderer.enabled} layer={HeroController.gameObject.layer} body={HeroController.rb2d.bodyType}"
***
